# Individual: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0001000> (out of scope)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0001000> "The term was added to the ontology on the assumption it was in scope, but it turned out later that it was not."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0001000> "This obsolesence reason should be used conservatively. Typical valid examples are: un-necessary grouping classes in disease ontologies, a phenotype term added on the assumption it was a disease."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0001000> <http://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432>)
